%I A401195 #15 Oct 29 2026 14:46:52
%S A401195 1,2,5,14,69,520,7075,177478,8454052
%N A401195 Number of connected unlabeled simple graphs on n vertices whose sandpile group is cyclic.
%C A401195 The sandpile group of a connected graph, also called its critical group or Jacobian, is the cokernel over the integers of a reduced graph Laplacian. It is cyclic exactly when at most one Smith invariant factor is greater than 1. The trivial group is cyclic, so all trees are counted.
%C A401195 Graphs are counted up to graph isomorphism. Nonisomorphic graphs with isomorphic sandpile groups are counted separately. A395521 counts the distinct groups that arise, up to group isomorphism.
%H A401195 R. Becker and D. Glass, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1504.05939">Cyclic Critical Groups of Graphs</a>, arXiv:1504.05939 [math.CO], 2015.
%H A401195 J. Clancy, T. Leake and S. Payne, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.3340">A note on Jacobians, Tutte polynomials, and two-variable zeta functions of graphs</a>, arXiv:1309.3340 [math.CO], 2013-2014.
%H A401195 J. Clancy, N. Kaplan, T. Leake, S. Payne and M. Wood, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1402.5129">On a Cohen-Lenstra Heuristic for Jacobians of Random Graphs</a>, arXiv:1402.5129 [math.CO], 2014-2015.
%H A401195 Sean A. Irvine, <a href="https://github.com/archmageirvine/joeis/blob/master/src/irvine/oeis/a401/A401195.java">Java program</a> (github)
%H A401195 Alexander Richard Towell, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23528939">Two exact statistics of graph sandpile groups at nine vertices</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%e A401195 For n=4 there are six connected graph classes. Only K_4 has a noncyclic sandpile group, namely Z/4 x Z/4. Thus a(4)=5.
%e A401195 For n=5 the count is 14, whereas A395521(5)=16 counts group types.
%Y A401195 Cf. A395521, A001349, A000055.
%K A401195 nonn,more,new
%O A401195 2,2
